    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Many a sunset has he watched lying on this rooftop, watching the sky turn from red to black, until the stars appear, before their light is overcome by the neon city.\nThe hour is early, and the sky should not look like dusk, but he pays little heed. Perhaps he considers it a sign of the coming of a kami.\nHe could not describe his own emotions as he gazes at the sky.\nExcitement? Anxiety? Fulfillment? Emptiness? Sadness?\nBut he lies there, waiting for a guest who may never come...\nUntil the warm breeze sends him into slumber."
